l according to the  defendant who had discussed directly had  been discussing divorce  um initially um  he he had brought up um divorce back in  2015 2016. um  they seemingly had worked through those  issues  and more recently uh maureen had brought  up that she wanted this divorce  as legal analyst dina dahl and co-host  terry austin terry what do you think  about the officer's explanation as to  when he gave  argy his miranda warnings  i think the officer actually gave a very  good explanation he said he was being  cautious he actually met with the  defendant in the hospital and he was  brought to the hospital while he was  with the police so  i think the officer was trying to say  that he wanted to make sure that the  defendant did not think he was in  custody there and he didn't want the  defendant to incriminate himself he  wanted to make sure that he understood  all his rights he wasn't under arrest  but he provided him with the miranda  rights just so at the end of the day  that interview would not be questioned  at any point in time so i thought it was  a good move make sense doubting your  eyes and crossing your teeth dina what  do you make of rg's reaction to his  wife's death and how will either side  argument  you know the defendant said that he  untied his wife because he didn't want  the children to see her like that and  then he went to this casino the judge  ruled that his fleeing the scene and  going to the casino can be used as  evidence for men's rhea for intent which  is very strong for the prosecution all  right we'll see how the prosecution uses  that information of course this is their  witness so obviously they think it's a  benefit to them but thank you both for  your input when we come back a 15 year  old suspect behind bars in the oxford  michigan school shooting we bring you  the latest on the deadly shooting as  authorities search for a motive  [Music]  welcome back new videos released showing  dozens of hours of interviews in the  andrew cuomo's sex crimes investigation  on monday the new york attorney  general's office released transcripts  and video interviews to the public from  an investigation that wrapped up in  august the video comes one month after a  criminal complaint was filed against the  former new york governor on charges of  sexual misconduct nearly a dozen women  both current and former employees of the  state have accused cuomo of sexual  harassment independent investigators  appointed by a new yorker attorney's  attorney general say cuomo did harass  multiple women hours of video testimony  show cuomo's reaction to the  investigation as he denied any  wrongdoing and said the alleged actions  could be based on perception  there was never a suggestion  that i wanted to date charlotte  all right i mean just to think about it  that was never  the concept of  grooming  nothing happened but i felt like we were  on a  path to something may be happening  she felt that way  i understand that i respect it  but this is all her perception right  cuomo resigned as governor in august  after a decade in office he is now  facing a misdemeanor sex crime complaint  that alleges he forcefully touched a  woman last december the latest now on a  school shooting in michigan a fourth  victim has now succumbed to their  injuries the shooting happened tuesday  afternoon at oxford high school about 45  minutes outside of detroit three  students were killed and a and several  more injured the fourth victim died on  wednesday investigators say they are  still trying to determine a motive for  the 15-year-old sophomore who opened  fire at his high school deputies  arrested the shooting suspect within  minutes of arriving at the school in  response to a flood of 9-1-1 calls  investigators reveal that his father  purchased a gun just days before the  shooting on black friday in a press  conference the oakland county sheriff  praised the quick emergency response  time  one of our deputies because of the  severity of wounds loaded up one of the  children in his car and sadly that child  died in the car  one of our employees who was in the 911  center as part of the team taking the  emergency calls  had a relative killed in the attack  and so this touches us all personally  and deeply and will for a long time this  wound will never go away  and we understand that but we also want  the community to know that we're here  for them  and we will leave no stone unturned in  determining all the things that led up  to it and making sure that this  investigation is full and complete  dina what do you think the investigation  to a mass shooting like this in michigan  will look like  i mean there's already quite a bit that  they know i mean this tragedy you know  occurred with these students who were  vulnerable and they saw this shooter the  shooter has been arrested it's true that  his parents aren't having him aren't  allowing him to be questioned by police  but there's already quite a bit that the  police know they know the gun that was  used and it was purchased by his father  so you know in terms of the  investigation there may be a little bit  more that they can find out in terms of  motive but they certainly already have  enough information absolutely especially  enough to at least go forward with some  initial charges terry he's just a high  school sophomore but  what is the prosecution against his team  going to look like and could the boy's  father face charges too  absolutely you know the prosecutor is  going after this with full force  charging him as an adult and they stated  the reason they're charging as an adult  is because the crime was so serious it  was not an impulsive act and so  the end of the day they shot 11 and  killed four and so the fact is the  parents could very well be brought in  you know that the parents you mentioned  brian bought the gun just very recently  they didn't protect the gun from their  son one of the things i'll also say is  during the arraignment they came on zoom  and they wore baseball caps to me that  is a sign of disrespect it does not seem  as though they are cooperating with the  authorities and based on all of that i  do think that if the prosecution can  find enough information against the  parents they too will be charged yeah  like you said not having protections for  the gun that could be a charge of itself  but thank you dean and terry and thank  you for joining us here on law on crime  daily we'll see you next time as we  discuss justice in america  [Music]  you
 

